WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.360
Hey what's up guys it's Rob, and welcome to&nbsp;
my tutorial for the Epic 2-in-1 Paper Cup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.240
Boomerang and Helicopter! Most people use their&nbsp;
cups to have a drink and throw it away. So I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.720
thought "Is there some way that we can get this&nbsp;
cup so that when you threw it away it actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.400
came back?!" Well after a few cuts and folds the&nbsp;
paper cup becomes a fun two-in-one model that not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.360
only spins down like a helicopter, but becomes an&nbsp;
amazing boomerang that comes back to you! It even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.840
has a ninja star on the back that I thought would&nbsp;
look really cool when I designed it. And of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.960
it's a great boomerang for doing trick shots. It&nbsp;
not only works with a variety of paper cups, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.080
you can also throw it with your left and right&nbsp;
hands--try throwing two at the same time! So get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.200
ready to learn the all-new Paper Cup Boomerang and&nbsp;
Helicopter. I'd like to take a moment to thank my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.000
new Patrons Ximena and Adam. It was fun teaching&nbsp;
you on Zoom. I showed them the boomerang on my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.640
Discord server and they definitely wanted to learn&nbsp;
it. If you want your chance to get a shout out, have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.760
your idea featured, access to my discord server,&nbsp;
or get one-on-one help and more head over to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.120
my Patreon and support me. For a limited time i'm&nbsp;
offering all new patrons a 30 minute zoom lesson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.200
You're going to need a paper cup and some&nbsp;
scissors. While it can work without tape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.520
some cups can be thicker or have outside&nbsp;
layers like these, making it harder to fold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.760
and it might require some tape just to hold&nbsp;
the flaps down. Plastic cups won't work for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.040
boomerang but can work for the helicopter but&nbsp;
not as well as paper. Pure styrofoam won't work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.720
but these paper coffee cups with paper inside and&nbsp;
soft foam exterior will work but might need tape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:40.320
because they don't fold as well as regular paper.&nbsp;
Once you have the proper supplies let's do it!&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:40.820
We need to first take the cup and cut it into&nbsp;
eight equal sections like this. To start,

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:51.200
we're going to hold it on two opposite sides and pull&nbsp;
apart and flatten it as best we can and make two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:57.040
really sharp pinches on the outside. We're only&nbsp;
folding the top of the rim not the entire cup. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.840
can take the scissors and cut the cup directly up&nbsp;
from the pinch in the rim all the way to the base&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:06.880
as straight as we can. Then we could do the same on&nbsp;
the opposite side, cutting it all the way from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.880
rim to the base. Now we could take the two edges of&nbsp;
each half and meet them together and make a pinch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.160
directly in the middle of the rim just like this.&nbsp;
Turn it around and do the same on the other side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.360
meeting the two cut corners or edges of the rim,&nbsp;
holding them together rounding it and giving it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.760
a pinch. Now, once again, we can cut it directly&nbsp;
on that pinch from the rim all the way to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:36.800
base on both sides. If it helps, you can make a mark&nbsp;
on the rim and draw a line to help you make nice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.640
straight cuts. Or sometimes the cup has patterns&nbsp;
you can use to guide you as well. To ensure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.880
you're cutting all the way to the bottom of the&nbsp;
inside, you could take the scissors and place them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.640
on the inside of the cup to see it going all the&nbsp;
way down to the base just like this. Now, we can cut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.080
the quarter sections into eighths by once again&nbsp;
folding the rim in half like this and making a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:04.960
pinch. Do that for all four pieces, trying to ensure&nbsp;
that they are folded exactly in half. Once you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:11.120
made a pinch on all four of the sections hold them&nbsp;
and just like before cut them in half, trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:17.120
divide them evenly down the middle of the section&nbsp;
so all eight pieces are about the same width.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:22.320
Take your time and try to cut as straight and&nbsp;
vertically as you can. When you're finished, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.520
should look like this and just make sure you cut&nbsp;
all the way to the base on the inside of the cup.&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.480
Now we're going to look for the section that&nbsp;
has the joint or lip in it and fold that down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.400
first. We're going to fold it down so that it is&nbsp;
flush completely with the base. It should fold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.280
down easily and you shouldn't hear any rips if&nbsp;
you did cut all the way to the bottom of the cup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.880
Then, we're going to skip every other section and&nbsp;
fold them down so that it's flat with the base.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:04:00.080
Continue until you have folded down four cup&nbsp;
sections and it should look just like this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.440
Now we could set it down on the table and flatten&nbsp;
the four sections which we just folded down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:09.920
I'm just going to make an "X" on the&nbsp;
sections we folded down with a marker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.720
Once we've done that, at this point this&nbsp;
is the "Helicopter Configuration" and if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.440
flip it over and spin it, it'll float down&nbsp;
as a helicopter, which i'll show a bit later (7:40)

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:28.240
At this point, we're going to fold down all of&nbsp;
the sections here.  The sections we marked with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.560
"X" are going to be the boomerang blades, while&nbsp;
the others are going to be interlocked like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.920
Ninja Star to create a "flap" or airfoil on each&nbsp;
blade.  Just like we did with the other sections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.640
fold down the last four sections and flatten&nbsp;
them out so they are even with the base.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.960
If you're having difficulty doing this, make sure&nbsp;
you cut far enough. Set it down on the table and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.600
make sure everything's nice and flat. Before you&nbsp;
try to make the boomerang, inspect it to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.960
the blades are relatively equal, flat and neat--not like this!  If it does you may want to toss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:03.081
it and try it again. Now, we can mark the other&nbsp;
sections 1 to 4 in a clockwise direction.&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.360
Then we can cut off the very tip of the rim on&nbsp;
only those numbered sections. Then we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:15.120
take the two opposite sections in this case 1&nbsp;(one)
and 3 (three) and fold them inwards with the bottom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:21.360
section folded UP on the left and the top section&nbsp;
folded DOWN on the right.  The inside edges should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:27.520
not be overlapped, but touching. Then we could turn&nbsp;
it and do the same with sections 2 (two) and 4 (four),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:31.760
folding them inwards the same exact way.&nbsp;
Once we've folded them in, we could press&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.320
down firmly. This is the same way that they&nbsp;
will be arranged when they are interlocked*&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.680
Now, we can open the numbered sections we just&nbsp;
folded inwards. We're going to now interlock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:47.120
them in a clockwise direction, starting with 1 (one)&nbsp;
and then moving to 2 (two), 3 (three) and so forth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:52.800
We're gonna first fold down 1 (one) so that the left&nbsp;
side of it is on the edge of the cup base.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.800 --> 00:06:01.520
Then, we're going to fold 2 (two) on top of it, and then&nbsp;
3 (three) down on top of 2 (two). Now, the last one 4 (four) is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:10.000
going to go on top of 3 (three) and underneath 1 (one). So&nbsp;
we're going to slide 1 (one) out from underneath 2 (two),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:17.120
just like this, and create a little pocket or an&nbsp;
opening, like a little bridge. Then we could round&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:24.240
4 (four) off and curve it a little bit at the end and&nbsp;
push it through the opening underneath 1 (one).&nbsp;

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.600
Once it's tucked under, you can grab it on the other&nbsp;
side and pull it all the way through. To make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.680
the sections are interlocked snugly, we're just&nbsp;
going to pull or tug on the two opposite sections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:41.680
to ensure that they're tucked in all the way and&nbsp;
secure. Just press down. When we've done that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:48.960
it should look something just like this. Now, you'll&nbsp;
see when we interlocked the sections on the back, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:54.400
created an overhang here on the other side of the&nbsp;
boomerang blades. You should notice that the flaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.000
will be counter-clockwise or on the left side of&nbsp;
the blade when they're facing directly upwards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.240
These will create an airfoil flap which we need to&nbsp;
fold down along the edge of the boomerang blade. &nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:12.320
So fold down all the way so that it's flush with the&nbsp;
top of the blade and make a nice sharp crease.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:18.160
We will do that now for the remaining three&nbsp;
airfoil flaps. Fold down along the top of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:24.240
blade and crease sharply. Finally, complete the last&nbsp;
one by folding it down and creasing and it should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.699
look something like this.

00:07:26.699 --> 00:07:32.900
If you find that the&nbsp;airfoils pop out
or stick up you can try taping them down at the very center here.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:37.795
Just wrap the&nbsp;
lower third (1/3) with tape to keep it flat and secure.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:44.240
To throw the helicopter, just make sure&nbsp;
that the four propellers are bent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:49.120
upwards like this and the other ones are&nbsp;
facing down and haven't been folded yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:57.840
Then, all you need to do is just throw it&nbsp;
from a height and give it a spin. So spin it!

00:08:15.354 --> 00:08:21.040
To throw the boomerang, I'm going to take it&nbsp;
like this. You can take it in your right hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:28.160
like this and hold it with your two fingers on top&nbsp;
and your thumb right on the airfoil here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:33.200
just like that. You can kind of rest it on the rest&nbsp;
of your fingers. I'm just going to flick my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:40.480
wrist out, I'm just going to snap my wrist like that.&nbsp;
So take it and just snap your wrist out like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.965
You can also take it in your hand on&nbsp;
one of the arms and flick it this way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:50.534
And you can use your left hand even&nbsp;
and just do the same kind of thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.840
It basically works with&nbsp;
all these different cups!

